      "id": "claim_4b889ad4e7864b418550fc212a31dc93",
      "statement": "The harness's gate verifiability doctrine requires every gate to enforce exactly one evidence tier — traceability (structure matches), provenance (evidence re-derived from the source of truth), or truth (behavior re-run) — and to document `Verifies:` and `Does not verify:` lines.",
